<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<circuit>
  <version>2</version>
  <attributes><entry><string>Width</string><int>8</int></entry><entry><string>Description</string><string>Hazard unit.  FWD0 and FWD1 select the source of rs1 and rs2 in EX.  FWD0 is 0 for the register file, 1 for the result in WB, and 2 for the result in MEM, which is newer; FWD1 counts down from 3 in the same order, for the reversed inputs of its mux.  STALL holds IF and DR for a cycle and sends a bubble to EX when DR reads the result of a load in EX.  FLUSH clears IF and DR when EX takes a branch or a jump.</string></entry></attributes>
